                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4226d1a-9318-3d4d-9dd9-9cfb842ffd83",
                                        "entry_id": "efad4e19-e026-30fc-b3f3-60216d6b11bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person confined to an institution such as a prison (as a convict) or hospital (as a patient)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a8170f1-31d5-30b0-b1b0-ed96615f566e",
                                        "entry_id": "efad4e19-e026-30fc-b3f3-60216d6b11bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who shares a residence (such as a hotel guest, a lodger, or a student living on campus), or other place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ac40cf4-73b7-4ee5-8a4c-e0e7ca8a73db",
                                                "sense_id": "4a8170f1-31d5-30b0-b1b0-ed96615f566e",
                                                "text": "[T]he inmates of the coach, by numerous hard, painful joltings, and ponderous, dragging trundlings, are suddenly made sensible of some great change in the character of the road."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28625b7d-1cca-31af-8c3d-4413afca9850",
                                        "entry_id": "efad4e19-e026-30fc-b3f3-60216d6b11bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of passenger, a person held or riding within a vehicle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6837aa7a-16df-495d-bdcc-63d363493381",
                                                "sense_id": "28625b7d-1cca-31af-8c3d-4413afca9850",
                                                "text": "P. della Valle writes in the same strain: \"And these two, the palankins and the andors [a kind of doli] also differ from one another, for in the andor the cane which sustains it is, as it is in the reti, straight; whereas in the palankin, for the greater convenience of the inmate, and to give more room for raising his head, the cane is arched upwards like this, _∩_...\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
